{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Assess one identified benefit offered by one actor in one promotion to one client; assess distinct benefits separately.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Read the generic wording in u14 within the circular’s SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A qualifying discount excludes that benefit only. A separate non-discount gift in the same promotion remains independently assessable.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Actual investor distraction is the stated rationale, not an additional factual prerequisite.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.6c0256c9bafa62f9e72fe4e8.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The formalization is a conditional reading of the retained standard; it does not establish temporal applicability or resolve missing authorities.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"1ced75d370b194c115b20946d8343dc198fe2b60cc3c4806e8a4b533cf409e58","candidate_id":"candidate.f45b3171601e4e4baf6279e9909ccfbc","controlled_language":"Selected control: paragraph-10 gift-offer restriction, fund-context reading. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, assess this restriction when the promotion concerns an SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such fund. If the intermediary offers a client a gift, the gift is not a discount of fees or charges, and its offer has the specified product or product-type promotional connection, the offer departs from the stated should-not-offer standard. Fund-house groupings can supply that connection. Structured-product status and proof of actual distraction are not prerequisites. Within scope, a true formal result flags tha